WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.026 --> 00:00:02.943
(triumphant music)

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.133
- [Voiceover] Hey and welcome!

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:10.766
I'm Hammeh, and in this series,

00:00:10.766 --> 00:00:13.127
we're discovering the lore,
back story and characters

00:00:13.127 --> 00:00:15.488
of Overwatch's heroes,
including more detail

00:00:15.488 --> 00:00:17.963
through their in-game voice
lines and interactions.

00:00:17.963 --> 00:00:20.667
Before any map starts during
the game on various triggers,

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:23.092
Overwatch heroes chatter
with and react to each other

00:00:23.092 --> 00:00:25.639
in some funny in-game voice interactions.

00:00:25.639 --> 00:00:26.699
These give us some great insights

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:29.688
into hero character,
interests and back stories.

00:00:29.688 --> 00:00:31.756
In this video, we're
looking at Junkrat's story

00:00:31.756 --> 00:00:33.263
through his interactions
with fellow heroes

00:00:33.263 --> 00:00:35.618
or villains and the world around him.

00:00:35.618 --> 00:00:37.231
An explosive obsessed freak who lives

00:00:37.231 --> 00:00:39.142
to cause chaos and destruction,

00:00:39.142 --> 00:00:40.442
Junkrat is currently on the run

00:00:40.442 --> 00:00:42.246
with his partner in crime, Roadhog,

00:00:42.246 --> 00:00:43.772
causing chaos around the world.

00:00:43.772 --> 00:00:45.855
Slightly radiation tinged and unhinged

00:00:45.855 --> 00:00:47.280
from his time as a Junker,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.697
Junkrat holds a valuable secret

00:00:48.697 --> 00:00:50.997
that bounty hunters and
nefarious individuals

00:00:50.997 --> 00:00:52.085
are hunting him for.

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:53.461
Whether we'll find out what it is in time

00:00:53.461 --> 00:00:54.912
remains to be seen.

00:00:54.912 --> 00:00:57.017
Firstly, we'll quickly run
through Junkrat's story.

00:00:57.017 --> 00:00:58.681
The first Omnic Crisis affected lives

00:00:58.681 --> 00:01:00.118
all around the world.

00:01:00.118 --> 00:01:02.262
When defunct, dismantled omniums,

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:04.838
massive factories of automated
construction machines

00:01:04.838 --> 00:01:06.834
and self-improving software algorithms

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:08.648
built by the Omnica Corporation,

00:01:08.648 --> 00:01:10.480
decided to wake themselves back up,

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.010
they launched a military campaign

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:13.220
against all of humanity.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.576
Australia wasn't spared.

00:01:14.576 --> 00:01:16.085
In the peace agreements
following the crisis,

00:01:16.085 --> 00:01:18.503
government officials gifted
the Australian omnium

00:01:18.503 --> 00:01:20.044
and the surrounding area to the Omnics

00:01:20.044 --> 00:01:21.739
that nearly destroyed their country,

00:01:21.739 --> 00:01:23.461
hoping to establish a
longtime peace accord.

00:01:23.461 --> 00:01:26.027
This arrangement permanently
displaced a large number

00:01:26.027 --> 00:01:28.099
of the Outback's residents,
a scattered collection of

00:01:28.099 --> 00:01:30.010
survivalists, solar farmers and people

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:31.987
who just wanted to be left alone.

00:01:31.987 --> 00:01:33.037
Furious over the loss of their homes,

00:01:33.037 --> 00:01:34.974
this group turned to violent rebellion.

00:01:34.974 --> 00:01:36.590
Events escalated until the rebels

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:38.545
sabotaged the omnium's fusion core,

00:01:38.545 --> 00:01:40.996
resulting in an explosion
that destroyed the facility,

00:01:40.996 --> 00:01:43.304
irradiated the region
and littered the Outback

00:01:43.304 --> 00:01:46.221
with twisted metal and
wreckage for kilometers around.

00:01:46.221 --> 00:01:47.054
Some people survived.

00:01:47.054 --> 00:01:47.993
Calling themselves the Junkers,

00:01:47.993 --> 00:01:49.537
they scavenged the husk of the omnium

00:01:49.537 --> 00:01:51.892
and formed a lawless, cutthroat
society in its shadow.

00:01:51.892 --> 00:01:52.899
Junkrat was one of them.

00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:54.720
He eked out a living by reclaiming metal

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.129
and components from the ruins.

00:01:56.129 --> 00:01:57.723
Like many others, he was affected

00:01:57.723 --> 00:01:59.023
by the lingering radiation.

00:01:59.023 --> 00:02:00.688
This touch of madness made him ideal

00:02:00.688 --> 00:02:02.158
for handling dangerous explosives,

00:02:02.158 --> 00:02:04.140
a love which he's turned into a bit

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:05.684
of an obsession, it's safe to say.

00:02:05.684 --> 00:02:07.101
Junkrat would have been
just another casualty

00:02:07.101 --> 00:02:09.254
of the war if he hadn't shot to notoriety

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:11.624
when he discovered an
extremely valuable secret

00:02:11.624 --> 00:02:13.766
in the bones of the Australian omnium.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:14.948
Few know the nature of what he's found,

00:02:14.948 --> 00:02:16.728
but he was pursued by bounty hunters,

00:02:16.728 --> 00:02:18.885
gangs and opportunists, wherever he went,

00:02:18.885 --> 00:02:19.940
until he struck a deal

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.528
with the Junker enforcer, Roadhog.

00:02:21.528 --> 00:02:23.725
Roadhog grudgingly bodyguards Junkrat

00:02:23.725 --> 00:02:26.140
in exchange for a 50-50
share of the spoils,

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:28.113
probably the only reason he puts up

00:02:28.113 --> 00:02:29.579
with the explosive obsessive.

00:02:29.579 --> 00:02:32.064
Now Roadhog in tow, Junkrat
has left the Outback

00:02:32.064 --> 00:02:34.012
and embarked upon an
international crime spree,

00:02:34.012 --> 00:02:36.730
leaving nothing but havoc
and bedlam in his wake.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:39.056
So far, we've seen the pair
in the UK. and King's Row

00:02:39.056 --> 00:02:40.259
stealing the Crown Jewels,

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:42.111
robbing in a vault in Dorado, Mexico,

00:02:42.111 --> 00:02:44.359
and even breaking into
ice cream trucks in Paris

00:02:44.359 --> 00:02:45.704
and robbing arcade toys

00:02:45.704 --> 00:02:47.428
in what might be Hanamura, Japan.

00:02:47.428 --> 00:02:49.119
We also know that Junkrat
and Roadhog have been

00:02:49.119 --> 00:02:50.598
to Sydney, as detailed in their comic,

00:02:50.598 --> 00:02:52.746
Going Legit, at some point,
when what they thought

00:02:52.746 --> 00:02:54.703
was a legitimate job
turned out to be a setup,

00:02:54.703 --> 00:02:56.373
they got an explosive revenge

00:02:56.373 --> 00:02:58.270
with the presumed death of the CEO

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.629
or a senior member of a
company called Hyde Global,

00:03:00.629 --> 00:03:02.036
as well as destroying a building

00:03:02.036 --> 00:03:03.737
in Sydney central business district.

00:03:03.737 --> 00:03:05.048
Even with a motto of no job too big,

00:03:05.048 --> 00:03:06.855
no score too small is there any reason

00:03:06.855 --> 00:03:08.763
for this trail of destruction and mayhem?

00:03:08.763 --> 00:03:09.703
Does it have anything to do

00:03:09.703 --> 00:03:11.308
with the treasure that Junkrat's hiding?

00:03:11.308 --> 00:03:13.519
Or are the two just,
well, enjoying themselves?

00:03:13.519 --> 00:03:15.910
With this mad pair, you
probably can't tell?

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:19.040
- [Junkrat] It's a perfect
day for some mayhem!

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:19.948
- [Voiceover] As you might expect

00:03:19.948 --> 00:03:21.065
for a crazy, explosive obsessive,

00:03:21.065 --> 00:03:22.748
Junkrat loves nothing more than talking

00:03:22.748 --> 00:03:24.307
about his favorite hobby.

00:03:24.307 --> 00:03:26.055
And that, of course, is blowing things up.

00:03:26.055 --> 00:03:27.496
- [Junkrat] You look like the kind of guy

00:03:27.496 --> 00:03:30.246
who could use something blown up!

00:03:31.791 --> 00:03:33.312
It's hard to just sit around,

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:34.722
knowing there's someone out there

00:03:34.722 --> 00:03:36.889
that needs to be blown up!

00:03:37.851 --> 00:03:39.418
If at first you don't succeed,

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:40.835
blow it up again!

00:03:42.277 --> 00:03:43.163
Oh, don't mind me.

00:03:43.163 --> 00:03:44.354
I was just taking five.

00:03:44.354 --> 00:03:46.175
Definitely not thinking
about blowing something up.

00:03:46.175 --> 00:03:47.417
No way!

00:03:47.417 --> 00:03:48.250
(laughs)

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.935
Definitely not!

00:03:49.935 --> 00:03:51.909
Okay, come on, maybe
just a little something?

00:03:51.909 --> 00:03:53.336
- [Voiceover] And when he's
not talking about his vocation,

00:03:53.336 --> 00:03:55.291
Junkrat's doing his second favorite thing

00:03:55.291 --> 00:03:56.124
or things in the world.

00:03:56.124 --> 00:03:58.068
Those are cracking bad
jokes and throwing insults.

00:03:58.068 --> 00:04:00.848
- [Junkrat] I've got a
leg up on the competition.

00:04:00.848 --> 00:04:03.053
Blew up just one.

00:04:03.053 --> 00:04:06.136
Don't you come the raw prawn with me!

00:04:07.016 --> 00:04:08.933
Ah, aiming's overrated.

00:04:10.069 --> 00:04:11.450
Outta my face, ya drongo!

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.354
- [Voiceover] While we're
on the subject of bad jokes,

00:04:13.354 --> 00:04:16.250
Junkrat loves to mock just
about anything and anyone.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:18.131
Stay tuned for a mini Junkrat quiz.

00:04:18.131 --> 00:04:20.105
Can you guess what
Junkrat is taking the mick

00:04:20.105 --> 00:04:21.666
out of in each of these lines?

00:04:21.666 --> 00:04:23.103
I'll give you the answers after each one.

00:04:23.103 --> 00:04:25.522
- [Junkrat] Baby, I'm a firework!

00:04:25.522 --> 00:04:26.909
- [Voiceover] That, of
course, is Katy Perry

00:04:26.909 --> 00:04:29.166
with her Firework song.

00:04:29.166 --> 00:04:31.022
- [Junkrat] And on that bombshell.

00:04:31.022 --> 00:04:31.995
- [Voiceover] That, of course, is

00:04:31.995 --> 00:04:33.815
Top Gear Jeremy Clarkson's
old sign off line

00:04:33.815 --> 00:04:36.348
at the end of every episode.

00:04:36.348 --> 00:04:39.274
- [Junkrat] Now, that's a knife!

00:04:39.274 --> 00:04:41.686
- [Voiceover] The infamous
knife scene in Crocodile Dundee,

00:04:41.686 --> 00:04:44.194
when they compare the
size of their knives.

00:04:44.194 --> 00:04:48.019
- [Junkrat] If I had PhD,
they'd call me Dr. Boom!

00:04:48.019 --> 00:04:50.202
- [Voiceover] Of course,
that's Dr. Boom from Area 52,

00:04:50.202 --> 00:04:51.553
Netherstorm in World of Warcraft,

00:04:51.553 --> 00:04:52.646
and since known as Dr. Balanced

00:04:52.646 --> 00:04:55.122
or Dr. Seven in Hearthstone.

00:04:55.122 --> 00:04:56.505
- [Junkrat] Time is money, friends.

00:04:56.505 --> 00:04:58.004
And we're almost flat broke!

00:04:58.004 --> 00:04:58.837
Attack!

00:04:59.992 --> 00:05:02.287
- [Voiceover] Time is money,
friends is a direct reference

00:05:02.287 --> 00:05:03.552
to the goblins in World of Warcraft.

00:05:03.552 --> 00:05:05.051
They say it all the time
when you click on them.

00:05:05.051 --> 00:05:06.690
Now, the last one of these
is really impressive.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.952
Thanks to our guest voiceover
for spotting this one.

00:05:08.952 --> 00:05:10.447
Where'd you think this music is from?

00:05:10.447 --> 00:05:12.154
Or how it's referring to Junkrat?

00:05:12.154 --> 00:05:13.474
♫ Dum, dum, dum, dum, dum

00:05:13.474 --> 00:05:15.764
♫ Dum, dum, dum, dum, dum ♫

00:05:15.764 --> 00:05:17.118
Now, I don't think that's in-game,

00:05:17.118 --> 00:05:18.992
but according to our guest voiceover,

00:05:18.992 --> 00:05:20.323
it's in V for Vendetta.

00:05:20.323 --> 00:05:21.645
Hugo Weaving actually wears

00:05:21.645 --> 00:05:23.598
a Guy Fawkes mask throughout the film.

00:05:23.598 --> 00:05:24.815
And this music is used in the final scene

00:05:24.815 --> 00:05:26.660
where the Houses of
Parliament get blown up.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:27.493
Spoiler.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:28.326
Do, of course, remember

00:05:28.326 --> 00:05:30.025
that Junkrat's name is Jamison Fawkes.

00:05:30.025 --> 00:05:31.630
Guy Fawkes blowing stuff up.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:33.070
Finally, this music is also used

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:34.301
in some fireworks displays

00:05:34.301 --> 00:05:35.740
and you can see fireworks with music.

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:37.156
So, multiple different references there

00:05:37.156 --> 00:05:38.039
in that little bit of music,

00:05:38.039 --> 00:05:38.976
very, very cool.

00:05:38.976 --> 00:05:41.929
Cheers to our guest voiceover
for spotting that one.

00:05:41.929 --> 00:05:43.536
Junkrat and Roadhog by knowing each other

00:05:43.536 --> 00:05:45.440
don't have huge connections
with the other cast

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:46.800
of Overwatch at the moment.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.224
But that does not stop Junkrat

00:05:48.224 --> 00:05:50.141
from liberally chatting
to and in some cases,

00:05:50.141 --> 00:05:51.708
mocking a lot of them.

00:05:51.708 --> 00:05:53.270
As we know, Junkrat and
Roadhog are literally

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:54.154
as thick as thieves.

00:05:54.154 --> 00:05:56.324
Roadhog's in it for the
money, guarding Junkrat

00:05:56.324 --> 00:05:57.729
for a half share of his treasure.

00:05:57.729 --> 00:05:59.143
And the two make quite the double act

00:05:59.143 --> 00:06:00.133
on some occasions.

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:01.862
Junkrat has a very literal view

00:06:01.862 --> 00:06:03.460
of the pair's relationship sometimes.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.237
- [Junkrat] You hook 'em, I'll cook 'em.

00:06:05.237 --> 00:06:06.774
- [Voiceover] And when
Roadhog asks Junkrat

00:06:06.774 --> 00:06:09.366
to stay out of trouble,
Junkrat swears he will.

00:06:09.366 --> 00:06:11.529
Maybe Roadhog's the father
figure in this team up.

00:06:11.529 --> 00:06:13.420
- [Junkrat] I'll be on me best behavior.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:14.591
- [Voiceover] Apparently,
Roadhog comes out

00:06:14.591 --> 00:06:16.019
with the odd joke even,
according to Junkrat.

00:06:16.019 --> 00:06:18.195
- [Junkrat] You won't
believe the joke old pig face

00:06:18.195 --> 00:06:19.917
over there told me the other day.

00:06:19.917 --> 00:06:20.990
Huh, Roadhog?

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:22.198
- [Voiceover] Ultimately,though,
we know Roadhog's

00:06:22.198 --> 00:06:23.732
a man of few words.

00:06:23.732 --> 00:06:25.810
When Junkrat sees an allied Roadhog

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:28.635
getting a kill on his team,
he expresses his thanks.

00:06:28.635 --> 00:06:30.679
- [Junkrat] I knew there was
a reason I kept you around.

00:06:30.679 --> 00:06:33.089
And it wasn't the sparkling conversation.

00:06:33.089 --> 00:06:34.594
- [Voiceover] Whatever barbs
he throws Roadhog's way,

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:36.635
Junkrat does care about
the fate of his bodyguard.

00:06:36.635 --> 00:06:38.180
When a Roadhog gets
killed on the same team

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:40.524
as a Junkrat, you might be able
to hear this line, I think.

00:06:40.524 --> 00:06:42.236
- [Junkrat] Ay, I'm the only one

00:06:42.236 --> 00:06:44.081
who gets to kill the big lug!

00:06:44.081 --> 00:06:44.914
- [Voiceover] And I have no idea

00:06:44.914 --> 00:06:45.747
when this line triggers,

00:06:45.747 --> 00:06:46.597
but it's kind of touching

00:06:46.597 --> 00:06:48.063
for Junkrat to say this to Roadhog.

00:06:48.063 --> 00:06:49.101
Don't you think?

00:06:49.101 --> 00:06:51.995
- [Junkrat] I could
always count on you, mate!

00:06:51.995 --> 00:06:53.631
- [Voiceover] Junkrat has a
few interactions with Mei.

00:06:53.631 --> 00:06:56.017
Even if he's trying to be
polite and make conversation,

00:06:56.017 --> 00:06:57.974
Mei doesn't really want to
have anything to do with him.

00:06:57.974 --> 00:07:00.411
- [Junkrat] I get cold just lookin' at ya.

00:07:00.411 --> 00:07:02.553
- [Mei] Then, you should
look somewhere else.

00:07:02.553 --> 00:07:04.012
- [Voiceover] And when
Mei criticizes Junkrat,

00:07:04.012 --> 00:07:05.702
his usual wit comes to his defense.

00:07:05.702 --> 00:07:07.677
Take your own pun medicine, Mei!

00:07:07.677 --> 00:07:09.631
- [Mei] You're just a no good bully!

00:07:09.631 --> 00:07:12.166
How can you even look at
yourself in the mirror?

00:07:12.166 --> 00:07:14.228
- [Junkrat] That's cold!

00:07:14.228 --> 00:07:15.319
- [Voiceover] As one of
the faces of Overwatch,

00:07:15.319 --> 00:07:17.682
Tracer is a prime target
for Junkrat's quips.

00:07:17.682 --> 00:07:20.329
Even her trademark catchphrase isn't safe.

00:07:20.329 --> 00:07:21.301
- [Junkrat] Cheers, mate!

00:07:21.301 --> 00:07:23.024
The cavalry's here.

00:07:23.024 --> 00:07:24.976
- [Tracer] That's my line.

00:07:24.976 --> 00:07:26.557
- [Voiceover] Now, Junkrat
probably regrets his rudeness

00:07:26.557 --> 00:07:29.088
when his curiosity about
explosives gets the better of him.

00:07:29.088 --> 00:07:30.213
- [Junkrat] Think I could have a look

00:07:30.213 --> 00:07:32.308
at one of those bombs of yours?

00:07:32.308 --> 00:07:34.075
- [Voiceover] As we've seen from his bio,

00:07:34.075 --> 00:07:35.486
Junkrat's no fan of Omnics.

00:07:35.486 --> 00:07:36.521
And I think this line triggers

00:07:36.521 --> 00:07:38.149
when he either gets hit or discord orbed

00:07:38.149 --> 00:07:39.326
from an enemy Zenyatta.

00:07:39.326 --> 00:07:40.449
There's a couple of variations.

00:07:40.449 --> 00:07:41.979
- [Junkrat] Piece of junk!

00:07:41.979 --> 00:07:43.040
- [Voiceover] Junkrat even finds it funny

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:44.595
when he sees one of himself.

00:07:44.595 --> 00:07:46.027
- [Junkrat] He looks familiar.

00:07:46.027 --> 00:07:47.807
Hey, that's me!

00:07:47.807 --> 00:07:49.042
- [Voiceover] And finally, I'm not sure

00:07:49.042 --> 00:07:50.502
of the trigger for this,
or if it's in-game,

00:07:50.502 --> 00:07:51.596
but it's kind of interesting to see

00:07:51.596 --> 00:07:53.712
how Junkrat sees himself anyway.

00:07:53.712 --> 00:07:54.849
- [Junkrat] I beg your pardon!

00:07:54.849 --> 00:07:57.217
I consider myself a freedom fighter,

00:07:57.217 --> 00:07:58.834
a misunderstood one.

00:07:58.834 --> 00:08:00.189
- [Voiceover] In the
last of our interactions,

00:08:00.189 --> 00:08:01.360
there's a couple of interactions

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:03.278
with other heroes around
Junkrat's treasure.

00:08:03.278 --> 00:08:04.136
Now, I don't have the lines on me,

00:08:04.136 --> 00:08:05.534
but Hanzo and apparently Reaper,

00:08:05.534 --> 00:08:06.873
but both ask him about his treasure

00:08:06.873 --> 00:08:09.026
with Hanzo saying you
couldn't possibly keep it

00:08:09.026 --> 00:08:10.505
on your person, apparently.

00:08:10.505 --> 00:08:11.462
Junkrat has a couple of responses

00:08:11.462 --> 00:08:12.625
to the two different individuals.

00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:13.815
Here's one of them.

00:08:13.815 --> 00:08:15.835
- [Hanzo] Where did
you hide your treasure?

00:08:15.835 --> 00:08:17.695
You could hardly have it on your person.

00:08:17.695 --> 00:08:19.153
- [Junkrat] Treasure?

00:08:19.153 --> 00:08:21.454
Sure I don't know anything
you're talking about!

00:08:21.454 --> 00:08:22.924
- [Voiceover] When it comes
to the world of Overwatch,

00:08:22.924 --> 00:08:24.878
we know that Junkrat and
Roadhog from their crime spree

00:08:24.878 --> 00:08:27.864
are pretty well-traveled
since leaving the Outback.

00:08:27.864 --> 00:08:29.695
So naturally, Junkrat's got a bunch to say

00:08:29.695 --> 00:08:30.913
on several maps.

00:08:30.913 --> 00:08:32.219
The tension between Omnics and humans

00:08:32.219 --> 00:08:34.602
in King's Row strikes a cord with Junkrat.

00:08:34.602 --> 00:08:36.439
He's, of course, had tensions with Omnics

00:08:36.439 --> 00:08:37.705
in his own life, too.

00:08:37.705 --> 00:08:39.485
Here's what he says when
he spawns on King's Row.

00:08:39.485 --> 00:08:40.629
- [Junkrat] So, we're delivering a bomb

00:08:40.629 --> 00:08:43.885
to scrap some bots, and
I'm getting paid for it.

00:08:43.885 --> 00:08:45.579
My kind of job.

00:08:45.579 --> 00:08:47.838
- [Voiceover] And as we've
seen in the Moment in Crime,

00:08:47.838 --> 00:08:49.423
the video about Junkrat and Roadhog,

00:08:49.423 --> 00:08:50.943
the two actually stole the Crown Jewels

00:08:50.943 --> 00:08:52.806
or definitely did some kind of heist here.

00:08:52.806 --> 00:08:54.142
And both of them will reminisce fondly

00:08:54.142 --> 00:08:55.899
about it in a couple of different ways.

00:08:55.899 --> 00:08:57.631
- [Junkrat] Ah, remember that time

00:08:57.631 --> 00:08:59.994
we stole the Crown Jewels.

00:08:59.994 --> 00:09:03.633
All hail King Jamison Fawkes the First.

00:09:03.633 --> 00:09:06.120
And, uh, Duke Roadhog?

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:08.419
What is your name anyways?

00:09:08.419 --> 00:09:10.337
God save the king!

00:09:10.337 --> 00:09:12.099
(laughs)

00:09:12.099 --> 00:09:13.846
- [Voiceover] Numbani, of
course, is meant to be the city

00:09:13.846 --> 00:09:15.907
where Omnics and humans
live together in harmony.

00:09:15.907 --> 00:09:18.640
And Junkrat naturally is
a little bit skeptical

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:20.119
to say the least about this.

00:09:20.119 --> 00:09:21.805
- [Junkrat] This place is the worst!

00:09:21.805 --> 00:09:24.648
Let's turn it into one big scrap heap.

00:09:24.648 --> 00:09:25.858
- [Voiceover] Really no fan of Omnics,

00:09:25.858 --> 00:09:27.434
as we can see several times.

00:09:27.434 --> 00:09:28.642
Dorado is quite closely linked

00:09:28.642 --> 00:09:29.656
to Junkrat and Roadhog.

00:09:29.656 --> 00:09:30.931
There's a whole bunch of evidence showing

00:09:30.931 --> 00:09:32.379
that they've robbed the bank,

00:09:32.379 --> 00:09:34.438
their faces on the
monitors here, for example,

00:09:34.438 --> 00:09:35.588
the bank heist map in the level

00:09:35.588 --> 00:09:37.648
that was also shown at Blizzcon 2015,

00:09:37.648 --> 00:09:38.762
I think in the lower panel,

00:09:38.762 --> 00:09:40.119
and the sprays of Junkrat and Roadhog,

00:09:40.119 --> 00:09:41.831
if you're very quick, that you can see

00:09:41.831 --> 00:09:44.903
in Soldier: 76's Hero short, on this wall.

00:09:44.903 --> 00:09:45.833
For my review of that short,

00:09:45.833 --> 00:09:47.905
check out the video on
the channel, linked below.

00:09:47.905 --> 00:09:48.843
Of course, when Junkrat returns

00:09:48.843 --> 00:09:49.835
to the scene of the crime,

00:09:49.835 --> 00:09:51.188
he does have a little reminisce

00:09:51.188 --> 00:09:52.889
and maybe wonders if he
needs a little bit more

00:09:52.889 --> 00:09:55.206
liquid cash assets, shall we say.

00:09:55.206 --> 00:09:56.989
- [Junkrat] Hey, me old tunnel!

00:09:56.989 --> 00:09:59.484
Might be time to make another withdrawal.

00:09:59.484 --> 00:10:00.389
- [Voiceover] Junkrat's no fan of Omnics,

00:10:00.389 --> 00:10:02.503
as we've seen in his
comic and in other lines,

00:10:02.503 --> 00:10:05.197
so visiting the home of
the Shambali in Nepal

00:10:05.197 --> 00:10:07.352
is naturally not going to
be to his liking at all.

00:10:07.352 --> 00:10:08.304
There's a couple of different lines

00:10:08.304 --> 00:10:09.338
associated with here,

00:10:09.338 --> 00:10:10.882
when Junkrat spawns and maybe another one

00:10:10.882 --> 00:10:11.929
I think as well.

00:10:11.929 --> 00:10:13.746
- [Junkrat] If these bots
wanna go into the light,

00:10:13.746 --> 00:10:16.340
I'd be more than happy to help.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:19.859
Now this place, bah, makes
me wanna be an atheist.

00:10:19.859 --> 00:10:21.096
- [Voiceover] Whatever his
feelings towards Omnics,

00:10:21.096 --> 00:10:22.535
Junkrat always defaults back

00:10:22.535 --> 00:10:23.700
to his trademark,

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:25.475
uh, entrepreneurship?

00:10:25.475 --> 00:10:26.846
He sees the business opportunities

00:10:26.846 --> 00:10:28.484
on the Temple of Anubis, sure enough,

00:10:28.484 --> 00:10:30.100
when you spawn him, as you should be able

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:30.933
to hear here.

00:10:30.933 --> 00:10:31.766
(gun fires)

00:10:31.766 --> 00:10:32.599
- [Junkrat] You think there's something

00:10:32.599 --> 00:10:35.114
worth stealing in that temple?

00:10:35.114 --> 00:10:36.259
- [Voiceover] Junkrat's
always appreciative

00:10:36.259 --> 00:10:37.503
of fellow craftsmen.

00:10:37.503 --> 00:10:38.959
When I say craftsmen, I mean people

00:10:38.959 --> 00:10:40.697
who can create chaos and destruction.

00:10:40.697 --> 00:10:42.933
And I think that this one
may well be on Route 66

00:10:42.933 --> 00:10:44.552
when he's looking at the right truck.

00:10:44.552 --> 00:10:45.540
- [Junkrat] Wow, look at this!

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.465
My hat's off to the architect

00:10:47.465 --> 00:10:49.936
of this fantastic destruction!

00:10:49.936 --> 00:10:51.427
- [Voiceover] And finally,
for fun, not heard this,

00:10:51.427 --> 00:10:53.630
but perhaps it's when Junkrat passes one

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.091
of the coffee shops in-game.

00:10:55.091 --> 00:10:55.924
Has anyone heard this one?

00:10:55.924 --> 00:10:58.006
- [Junkrat] Can you do a flat white?

00:10:58.006 --> 00:11:01.551
No, how 'bout I flatten the place?

00:11:01.551 --> 00:11:02.781
- [Voiceover] Thanks very much for tuning

00:11:02.781 --> 00:11:04.192
into my hero voice line and story series.

00:11:04.192 --> 00:11:05.760
Check out the playlist
linked here on the left

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:07.844
for more videos like
this of different heroes.

